# Story 38: Chat Mode (40s)
# Hook: The at-sign prompt is chat mode -- a conversation lane separate from prompt mode.
# Duration: 40s
# Source: story-038-chat-mode.tape
#
# Voiceover script with timing cues.
# Format: [START --> END] narration text
# Each entry should be spoken within its time window.
# Gaps between entries are silent (viewer watches the demo).
#
# Total segments: 5

[00:00.0 --> 00:03.0]
The at-sign prompt is chat mode -- a conversation lane separate from prompt mode.

[00:03.0 --> 00:09.0]
Start rysh in shell mode, then we'll cycle all the way around to chat.

[00:09.0 --> 00:20.0]
Double-Escape moves through prompt and rysh, then lands on the at-sign marker -- that's chat mode, for sending messages to AI chat.

[00:20.0 --> 00:32.0]
Chat keeps its own per-mode buffer, distinct from prompt mode's stream. Type a message and send it.

[00:32.0 --> 00:40.0]
Chat and prompt are separate streams in the same pane -- one for quick conversation, one for agentic work. Double-Escape returns you to shell.

